---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = "/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-klaviyo";
const title = "Yotpo Email & SMS to Klaviyo: Shopify migration decisions";
const desc = "Plan Shopify data, retained Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty connections, and explicit flow ownership when moving messaging to Klaviyo.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Must I remove Yotpo Reviews when moving to Klaviyo?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo documents an integration for review and loyalty data. Verify its configuration and assign review-request ownership before enabling replacement flows."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I reuse the old Yotpo migration connection?",
    "answer": "Do not assume a historical migration route remains available after decommissioning. Establish accessible records and current destination support before relying on that route."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p></header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>The comparison has become a migration decision</h2>
      <p>Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. Its live lifecycle notice says the dashboard and associated background services are inactive. Keeping Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty does not restore messaging. Evaluate a replacement sender while treating those retained products as separate services; the old suite-versus-standalone recommendation no longer describes an available choice.</p>
      <h2>Decide which system owns each customer field</h2>
      <p>Klaviyo documents a Shopify integration and warns that Shopify-synced properties can overwrite edits made inside Klaviyo. Treat Shopify tags as store-owned inputs when using them for exclusions. Rehearse a tag change in Shopify and inspect the destination profile before using it in a live flow. Keep imported legacy attributes separate from current store fields so historical Yotpo status cannot silently override current eligibility.</p>
      <h2>Retain Yotpo Reviews through a documented integration</h2>
      <p>Yotpo documents syncing review and loyalty data to Klaviyo. That gives an existing Yotpo merchant a supported direction to investigate without replacing review display merely to move email. Inspect the connected account, customer match and actual fields or events available. Choose one owner for review requests, then confirm that a submitted review prevents an inappropriate repeat ask. Integration availability is not proof that every old template or review block transfers unchanged.</p>
      <h2>Treat loyalty connection and loyalty messaging separately</h2>
      <p>Yotpo has current OAuth guidance for its Klaviyo Loyalty integration alongside legacy API-key documentation. Follow the guide for the connection you actually use. Rehearse a tier change and a redeemed reward before sending balance or eligibility claims. Keep the source of truth in the loyalty program and assign responsibility for handling absent or stale properties. Connecting data does not automatically retire existing Loyalty notifications.</p>
      <h2>Rebuild browse and recovery with clear exits</h2>
      <p>Inventory which Shopify events and onsite tracking your intended flow requires. Separate browse interest, cart activity and checkout abandonment instead of copying a single generic recovery sequence. In a proposed rehearsal, complete a purchase after entering a flow and inspect pending messages. Keep any promotional incentive consistent with margin policy. No source on this page establishes a recovery-rate ranking or predicts that a more detailed flow will outperform a simpler one.</p>
      <h2>Budget the stack you will operate</h2>
      <p>Decide whether email and SMS both move, and obtain current terms for the required profiles, sends, channel coverage and retained Yotpo products. Include the work of rebuilding forms, authenticating the sender and maintaining review and loyalty mappings. A store without existing Yotpo modules need not add them simply to justify this migration. An existing merchant should judge each retained module by the work it still performs, not by a former bundle discount.</p>
      <h2>Reconstruct the program from accessible records</h2>
      <p>Start with prior exports, saved templates, consent evidence, suppression records and Shopify data you can legitimately access. Do not promise a fresh export from the retired Yotpo dashboard. Ask support what recovery remains possible before setting a launch date. A customer email or phone number in an order record does not establish marketing permission. Preserve opt-outs and mark unknown consent for review rather than importing every customer as subscribed.</p>
      <h2>Activate against a message ownership map</h2>
      <p>List welcome, cart, checkout recovery, post-purchase education, review collection, loyalty notices and winback separately. Prepare replacement messages disabled and inspect purchase exits, opt-outs and missing fields before activation. Give each trigger one live owner, including Shopify automations and retained Yotpo modules. Record who can pause each sender if a customer receives the wrong sequence. These are proposed acceptance exercises, not tests we ran or evidence of revenue lift.</p>
      <h2>Primary sources</h2>
      <p>Product information checked November 25, 2026. <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo lifecycle notice</a> · <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005080407">Klaviyo Shopify setup</a> · <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/integrations/klaviyo/">Yotpo Klaviyo integration</a> · <a class="link" href="https://support.yotpo.com/docs/klaviyo-oauth-integration-yotpo-loyalty-referrals">Current Loyalty OAuth guide</a></p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Klaviyo vs Yotpo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">Yotpo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc">Reviews & UGC playbook</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/jewelry">Email apps for jewelry stores</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Migration questions" />
</BaseLayout>
